% Misuse: wrong types, wrong values, wrong shapes.
%
% Arity lives in 11-arity.selt; this file is everything else you can do wrong.
% It is organised by the Args accessor that rejects the argument, because that is
% the layer the error actually comes from — see docs/EXTENDING.md, "The Args API".
%
% Every case pins `at line:col`. The position is the promise: spec/errors.md says
% an error is raised at the innermost point of failure, so a bad argument must
% report *that argument's* position and not the call's. That promise had almost
% no coverage before this file, and it is exactly what drifts — the C++ host once
% reported the right operand's position for a left operand's type error, because
% argument evaluation order is unspecified there.
%
% Every expectation here was confirmed identical across all five implementations
% before being written down. None of these is one host's opinion.

%
% --- text(i) — E_NOT_TEXT
%
% Every built-in argument that goes through Args::text(). BOOL and BIN are the
% two kinds that reach it and cannot satisfy it.
### name: mis.not-text.len
--- source
LEN(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:5
===
### name: mis.not-text.left
--- source
LEFT(TRUE, 1)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:6
===
### name: mis.not-text.right
--- source
RIGHT(TRUE, 1)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:7
===
### name: mis.not-text.substr
--- source
SUBSTR(TRUE, 1)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:8
===
### name: mis.not-text.find-needle
--- source
FIND(TRUE, "a")
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:6
===
### name: mis.not-text.find-hay
--- source
FIND("a", TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:11
===
### name: mis.not-text.replace-needle
--- source
REPLACE(TRUE, "a", "b")
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:9
===
### name: mis.not-text.replace-with
--- source
REPLACE("a", TRUE, "b")
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:14
===
### name: mis.not-text.replace-hay
--- source
REPLACE("a", "b", TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:19
===
### name: mis.not-text.split-hay
--- source
SPLIT(TRUE, ",")
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:7
===
### name: mis.not-text.split-sep
--- source
SPLIT("a", TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:12
===
### name: mis.not-text.trim
--- source
TRIM(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:6
===
### name: mis.not-text.ltrim
--- source
LTRIM(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:7
===
### name: mis.not-text.rtrim
--- source
RTRIM(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:7
===
