%
% --- bool(i) — E_NOT_BOOL
%
% There is no truthiness anywhere in SEL, in functions or in operators.
### name: mis.not-bool.if-text
--- source
IF("x", 1, 2)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:4
===
### name: mis.not-bool.if-num
--- note
1 is not true. SEL has no truthiness, so a condition that is not BOOL is an
error rather than a coercion.
--- source
IF(1, 1, 2)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:4
===
### name: mis.not-bool.cond-first
--- source
COND("x", 1, 2)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:6
===
### name: mis.not-bool.cond-second
--- source
COND(FALSE, 1, "x", 2, 3)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:16
===
### name: mis.not-bool.all-body
--- source
ALL((1), _)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:10
===
### name: mis.not-bool.any-body
--- source
ANY((1), _)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:10
===
### name: mis.not-bool.filter-body
--- source
FILTER((1), _)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:13
===
### name: mis.not-bool.and-right
--- source
TRUE AND "x"
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:10
===
### name: mis.not-bool.or-left
--- source
"x" OR TRUE
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:1
===
### name: mis.not-bool.xor-left
--- source
1 XOR TRUE
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:1
===
### name: mis.not-bool.not-operand
--- source
NOT 1
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:5
===

%
% --- dec(i) — E_NOT_NUM
%
% Numbers are TEXT that parses as a number (§4). BOOL, BIN and text that does not
% parse all fail here.
### name: mis.not-num.abs-bool
--- source
ABS(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:5
===
### name: mis.not-num.abs-text
--- source
ABS("x")
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:5
===
### name: mis.not-num.abs-untrimmed
--- note
No implicit trimming: " 2" is text that happens to look numeric, and
accepting it would make whitespace silently significant (§4).
--- source
ABS(" 2")
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:5
===
### name: mis.not-num.abs-bin
--- source
ABS(TO_UTF8("1"))
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:5
===
### name: mis.not-num.sign
--- source
SIGN(TRUE)
--- expect
error E_NOT_NUM at 1:6
===
